    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The data includes Image Biomarker Standardization Initiative-based PyRadiomics features from the Quantitative Image Feature Pipeline (qifp.stanford.edu) for T2- and contrast enhanced T1-MRI of pre-operative patients undergoing resection for newly diagnosed pediatric medulloblastoma. Additional clinical features include age of diagnosis, gender, and molecular subgroup (WNT, SHH, Group 3 and Group 4.\r\n\r\nThe inclusion criteria were: consecutive patients with pathologically-confirmed MB that spanned July 1997 to May 2020, aged ≤ 19 years, with pre-operative MRI that included both axial contrast-enhanced T1-weighted (T1-MRI) and T2-weighted (T2-MRI) sequences, and molecular subgroup analysis. We excluded patients if the MRI was non-diagnostic or lacked MB molecular subgroup diagnosis.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Zhang, Michael and Wong, Samuel and Wright, Jason and Wagner, Matthias and Toescu, Sebastian and Han, Michelle and Tam, Lydia and Zhou, Quan and Ahmadian, Saman and Shpanskaya, Katie and Lummus, Seth and Lai, Hollie and Eghbal, Azam and Radmanesh, Alireza and Nemelka, Jordan and Harward, Stephen and Malinzak, Michael and Laughlin, Suzanne and Perreault, Sebastien and Braun, Kristina and Lober, Robert and Cho, Yoon Jae and Ertl-Wagner, Birgit and Ho, Chang and Mankad, Kshitij and Vogel, Hannes and Cheshier, Samuel and Jacques, Thomas and Aquilina, Kristian and Fisher, Paul and Taylor, Michael and Poussaint, Tina and Vitanza, Nicholas and Grant, Gerald and Pfister, Stefan and Thompson, Eric and Jaju, Alok and Ramaswamy, Vijau and Yeom, Kristen. (2021). Radiogenomics of Pediatric Medulloblastoma: A Multicenter Study. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/pq109xz1689",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
